refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public static Time\DurationTime\Duration::fromSeconds intseconds intnanoseconds0
Creates a non-negative duration of seconds seconds plus nanoseconds nanoseconds.

&reftitle.errors;
If seconds is negative, a ValueError is thrown.
If nanoseconds is negative, a ValueError is thrown.
If nanoseconds is greater than or equal to 1000000000, a ValueError is thrown.
&ext.datetime.duration-too-long;

  &reftitle.examples;

   Time\Duration::fromSeconds example


<?php
var_dump(\Time\Duration::fromSeconds(90));
var_dump(\Time\Duration::fromSeconds(1, 500_000_000));

try {
    \Time\Duration::fromSeconds(0, 1_000_000_000);
} catch (ValueError $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
}


   &example.outputs;


